@startuml PayLink_Payment_State_Diagram_Phase1

title PayLink - Payment Lifecycle State Machine (Phase 1)
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #333333
  FontColor #111111
}

[*] --> Initiated

Initiated --> Rejected : Fraud check fails\nor funds insufficient
Initiated --> FundsHeld : Fraud checks pass\nand wallet has enough funds
FundsHeld --> SentToBiller : Payment request sent
SentToBiller --> Completed : Biller confirms
SentToBiller --> Failed : Biller refuses
SentToBiller --> Unknown : No answer within 10 seconds\n(live biller)
Unknown --> Completed : Biller later confirms\n(callback, retry or settlement file)
Unknown --> Failed : Biller later refuses, or\nreconciliation confirms no payment
Failed --> Refunded : Hold successfully released

Completed --> [*]
Rejected --> [*]
Refunded --> [*]

note right of Unknown
  Funds remain held while the outcome is uncertain.
  Re-query after 1, 5 and 15 minutes from entering Unknown.
  After three unsuccessful re-queries, wait for reconciliation.
  Never refund Unknown automatically.

  TopUpNet's "accepted" response is not final; the payment
  remains SentToBiller until the callback. A callback-wait
  timeout is an open configurable policy (AMB-16).
end note

note bottom of Failed
  The hold release must succeed before Refunded is entered.
  This is an automatic release after confirmed biller failure,
  not the separate FR-27 customer refund request for a
  Completed payment. Completed remains a final state.
end note

note bottom of Completed
  Completed, Rejected and Refunded are final states.
  No Completed -> Refunded lifecycle transition is allowed.
end note

@enduml
